# =============================================================================
# Example: why the API key does not belong in .env
# =============================================================================
# dsh reads the DeepSeek API key from $DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml, written by the
# UI under Settings -> Models. The image deliberately does not read
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY from the environment: the inherited environment outranks the
# credentials file, so exporting it here would hide whether the file path works —
# which is the only thing the image's "test" stage exists to prove.
#
# So there is nothing to put in this file. Kept as documentation for the question
# "can I just export the key?" — no.
